{
  "_comment": "NOT NEEDED FOR NORMAL USE, AND UNVERIFIED. On firmware 1.50+ the board becomes two game controllers simply by switching to Dinput mode (hold Start1+P1SW2 for 10 seconds); the pin-to-button mapping is internal and the config block is not involved - a keyboard-mode dump and a Dinput-mode dump are byte-identical. This file exists only for the untested case of wanting custom per-pin gamepad button assignments.",
  "_sticks_note": "Stick pins (1up/1down/1left/1right, 2up/...) carry a description but no action on purpose. Pins a profile does not assign an action to keep whatever the board already has, so this file will not break your sticks. The descriptions record what Batocera expects each direction to be; whether the board wants HAT 0..3, ANALOG 0..7 or GAMEPAD codes to produce it is the open question the dump diff answers - add an \"action\" to these four pins per player once known.",
  "_description_note": "\"description\" is a label only. It is what the web UI shows next to the pin; the board is programmed from \"action\". Both players send GAMEPAD 1..12 because in Dinput mode each player is a separate controller and the two share one code range - the GP1/GP2 prefix is for the reader, not the board.",
  "schemaVersion": 2.0,
